    "hypothesis": "Hypothesis: hidden gate 557 = ReLU(1.283*oldpeak + 0.559*thal:7 - 1.076*slope:3 - 0.417*fbs:0 + 0.085) is a one-sided ischaemia-evidence detector. It switches on mainly with exercise-induced ST depression (oldpeak), more readily when there is a reversible thal defect (thal:7), is pushed down by a downsloping ST segment (slope:3, which is clinically counter-intuitive; it is rare, 7%, and the direct linear core has no slope:3 term, so this is probably how the network absorbs slope:3 at all), and slightly by normal fasting sugar (fbs:0). It enters the logit with weight +0.746, so it only ever adds risk. Evidence (train, n=242): closed form exact (single ReLU); active on 47.9% of patients (83% with thal:7, 27% without); max 4.72, logit contribution SD 0.78; sensitivity oldpeak 0.62 > slope:3 0.52 > thal:7 0.27 > fbs:0 0.20; replacing it by its mean drops train AUC of the logit from 0.947 to 0.938, the largest of the three gates.",
