    "hypothesis": "Hypothesis: hidden gate 1239 = ReLU(0.571*sex:0 + 0.903*exang:1 - 0.853) is a Boolean AND of female sex (sex:0) and exercise-induced angina (exang:1). Evidence (train, n=242): truth table of the standardised one-hot inputs gives activation 1.199 for women with exang (n=31, positive rate 63%) and exactly 0 for the other three cells (male/no exang n=96 pos 40%; male/exang n=63 pos 76%; female/no exang n=64 pos 14%; the male+exang pre-activation is -0.004, just below the threshold). Weighted +1.730 into the logit it adds +2.07, which cancels most of the direct female protective term (-1.573*sex:0 contributes -2.18 for women vs +1.14 for men): the network learns that exercise angina erases the female advantage. Active on 7.9% of patients, logit contribution SD 0.56; mean-ablation drops train AUC 0.947 -> 0.940. Closed form exact.",
