    "hypothesis": "Hypothesis: a protective high-exercise-capacity gate. Serial chain thal:3 -> 3818 -> 2124. 3818 = ReLU(1.003*thal:3 - 0.192) is a normal-thallium indicator taking only the values 0 (abnormal thal) and 0.702 (normal thal, 56% of patients). 2124 = ReLU(1.338*thalach + 0.763*cp:3 - 0.108*3818 - 0.932) fires when maximum heart rate is high, much more readily with non-anginal chest pain (cp:3): active on 80% of cp:3 patients but 10.5% of others (30.6% overall, max 2.88). It enters the logit with weight -0.918, so it only ever lowers risk, adding a hinge to the direct linear thalach (-0.470) and cp:3 (-0.743) terms. The thal:3 branch only moves the threshold by -0.076 (sensitivity 0.025 vs thalach 0.41, cp:3 0.23) and is nearly inert. Evidence (train, n=242): closed form exact; logit contribution SD 0.49; mean-ablation drops train AUC only 0.947 -> 0.945, the weakest of the three gates.",
