    "hypothesis": "Root hypothesis: an additive composition that is essentially logistic regression plus three one-sided ReLU corrections. Logit z = -0.680 + LINEAR CORE + 0.746*st_depression_gate + 1.730*female_exang_and_gate - 0.918*thalach_cp3_protective_gate, and the prediction is sigmoid(z) (get_formula renders the output as ReLU, but for this binary task the model applies a sigmoid to the output pre-activation). LINEAR CORE = 19 direct input->output edges, dominated by ca (+2.607, number of vessels), sex:0 (-1.573, women lower risk), chol (+0.870), slope:1 (-0.833, upsloping ST protective), cp:1 (-0.785), slope:2 (+0.743), cp:3 (-0.743), fbs:0 (+0.627), trestbps (+0.519), thal:7 (+0.490), thalach (-0.470), sex:1 (+0.390), thal:4 (+0.383), thal:6 (-0.351), cp:4 (+0.312); age, restecg:0, exang:0/1 near zero. cp:2, fbs:1, restecg:1, restecg:2 are unused. Corrections: (a) ischaemia evidence (ST depression, reversible thal defect) adds risk; (b) women with exercise angina lose most of their sex protection (AND gate, +2.07 logit); (c) high max heart rate, especially with non-anginal pain, removes extra risk. Evidence (train, n=242): accuracy 0.876, AUC 0.947. Linear core logit SD 4.90 vs gates 0.78 / 0.56 / 0.49. Linear core alone AUC 0.930; mean-ablating each gate gives AUC 0.938 / 0.940 / 0.945, so together the nonlinear parts add ~+0.017 train AUC. SHAP (probability scale): ca 0.170 >> sex:0 0.080 > slope:1 0.063 > cp:3 0.058 > slope:2 0.053 > thal:7 0.050 > chol 0.038 > thalach 0.034 > oldpeak 0.029. Function preservation of the refactored model 1.8e-15; all leaf closed forms exact up to 3-s.f. display rounding (max 0.027).",
